WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:08.920
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:16.134
Unit twenty-three: Grammar and Collocation. Today you will choose the natural word partners.

4
00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:19.202
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:23.191
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.190
Collocation.

7
00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:29.019
Collocation means words that naturally go together.

8
00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:31.686
Strong coffee is a collocation.

9
00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:34.924
Your turn. Say: Collocation.

10
00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:38.919
Collocation.

11
00:00:39.683 --> 00:00:40.928
Make a decision.

12
00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:44.810
Make a decision means the natural partner of decision.

13
00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:46.905
I must make a decision.

14
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:50.691
Your turn. Say: Make a decision.

15
00:00:53.533 --> 00:00:54.639
Make a decision.

16
00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:56.512
Do research.

17
00:00:57.517 --> 00:01:00.259
Do research means the natural partner of research.

18
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.583
She does research on bees.

19
00:01:03.183 --> 00:01:05.569
Your turn. Say: Do research.

20
00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:09.539
Do research.

21
00:01:10.283 --> 00:01:11.818
Take responsibility.

22
00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:15.722
Take responsibility means accept blame or duty.

23
00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:17.921
He took responsibility.

24
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:21.506
Your turn. Say: Take responsibility.

25
00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.983
Take responsibility.

26
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:27.741
Pay attention.

27
00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.144
Pay attention means to listen carefully.

28
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.320
Pay attention in class.

29
00:01:33.917 --> 00:01:36.592
Your turn. Say: Pay attention.

30
00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:40.481
Pay attention.

31
00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:42.171
Heavy rain.

32
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:45.705
Heavy rain means the natural partner of rain.

33
00:01:46.317 --> 00:01:48.049
Heavy rain fell all day.

34
00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.209
Your turn. Say: Heavy rain.

35
00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.195
Heavy rain.

36
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.346
Strong coffee.

37
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.267
Strong coffee means the natural partner of coffee.

38
00:02:01.883 --> 00:02:03.418
I like strong coffee.

39
00:02:04.017 --> 00:02:06.971
Your turn. Say: Strong coffee.

40
00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:11.148
Strong coffee.

41
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:12.861
Natural.

42
00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.952
Natural means sounding right to native speakers.

43
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.143
A natural combination.

44
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.799
Your turn. Say: Natural.

45
00:02:24.633 --> 00:02:25.565
Natural.

46
00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:30.099
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:36.142
Visal, why do we say heavy rain and strong coffee, not strong rain and heavy coffee?

48
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:48.055
Because of collocation. Some words naturally combine, and learners must memorise them as units. There is no logical rule; it is just the natural choice.

49
00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.720
Which verbs are tricky?

50
00:02:51.817 --> 00:03:03.902
Make and do. We make a decision, make progress, make a mistake. We do research, do homework, do business. Also take responsibility, pay attention, give advice.

51
00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:06.169
How do I learn them?

52
00:03:07.283 --> 00:03:21.223
Learn nouns with their verbs and adjectives, and record whole chunks in a notebook. Reading and listening show collocations in context. Using a collocation dictionary also builds your natural fluency.

53
00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:24.041
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:24.883 --> 00:03:30.726
Grammar focus: Collocation: verb plus noun and adjective plus noun combinations.

55
00:03:31.026 --> 00:03:32.155
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.722
She made an important decision.

57
00:03:35.617 --> 00:03:37.860
He does research on climate change.

58
00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.181
We had heavy rain all night.

59
00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:49.565
Learn word partners as chunks: make a decision, do research, take responsibility, pay attention, heavy rain, strong coffee.

60
00:03:50.317 --> 00:03:53.596
Be careful! Don't say: I did a decision.

61
00:03:55.533 --> 00:03:57.544
Say: I made a decision.

62
00:03:57.844 --> 00:03:59.264
Use make a decision.

63
00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:02.452
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:04.976
Words That Belong Together.

65
00:04:05.276 --> 00:04:07.647
I need to make a decision before Friday.

66
00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:11.039
Our class does research on local history.

67
00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:15.171
Everyone must take responsibility for their actions.

68
00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.445
Please pay attention to the instructions.

69
00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:21.526
Heavy rain made the road dangerous.

70
00:04:22.633 --> 00:04:26.531
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:27.383 --> 00:04:29.406
I must blank a decision today.

72
00:04:29.706 --> 00:04:32.570
A, do. B, make. C, take.

73
00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:37.703
The answer is B: make.

74
00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.302
She blank research on coral reefs.

75
00:04:41.602 --> 00:04:45.279
A, does. B, makes. C, gives.

76
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:50.798
The answer is A: does.

77
00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.032
Which is natural?

78
00:04:53.332 --> 00:04:57.508
A, strong rain. B, heavy rain. C, big rain.

79
00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.380
The answer is B: heavy rain.

80
00:05:04.517 --> 00:05:06.725
Collocations should be learned as blank.

81
00:05:07.025 --> 00:05:11.515
A, chunks. B, single words. C, rules.

82
00:05:15.067 --> 00:05:17.043
The answer is A: chunks.

83
00:05:18.183 --> 00:05:21.170
According to the reading, what did heavy rain make dangerous?

84
00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:25.204
A, the road. B, the river. C, the school.

85
00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:30.708
The answer is A: the road.

86
00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.750
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:35.583 --> 00:05:38.430
Which English collocations do you find surprising?

88
00:05:47.217 --> 00:05:48.694
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:48.994 --> 00:06:01.111
I find it surprising that we say heavy rain but strong coffee. Also we make a mistake but do homework. I try to learn these collocations as chunks, because the rules are not logical.

90
00:06:01.411 --> 00:06:03.213
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:04.117 --> 00:06:11.297
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and collocation: verb plus noun and adjective plus noun combinations.

92
00:06:11.597 --> 00:06:15.735
Today's value is lifelong learning. Keep learning for as long as you live.

93
00:06:16.035 --> 00:06:19.048
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:19.348 --> 00:06:21.895
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

